It's based on item probabilities. The odds that there are no enchant
armour scrolls in a full game down to the Valley are absolutely minute.

I've just jiggered a 3.4.3 installation so that a) it reports every time
an enchant armour scroll is generated, b) every time you search you
fall down a dungeon level, and c) every time you do that it kills all the
monsters on the level (this still omits death drops from later-generated
monsters in a real game). It is easy with this tool to see how many
scrolls would be generated on a run down to the Valley.

The results were: 2, 1, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 3, 1 from ten runs. That's ten
games which neither explored the Mines nor Sokoban, and which did not get
the death drops from 32K turns of monster generation. Since monsters are
made 1 turn in 70 in average, and the Mines and Sokoban are both rich with
items and monsters, there's a lot missing from those tallies.

Conversely the odds that a particular player misses objects or does not
efficiently preserve them for identification (especially one who doesn't
make stashes) are not minute at all.
